// What `<<| t, m` hands back for each key a GUI-style editor needs.
//
// Hypotheses DIS-ZYE-001, 002 and 003 (HALLAZGOS.md). Reads nineteen keys and
// prints the code point of each and its modifiers, `code:m`, separated by
// spaces. check.py sends the keys through a real pty — `--keys` hands the
// program keys that are already decoded, and the decoding is what is asked.
//
// Until 2026-11-22 this read `<<| t`, with no modifiers: there was no form to
// read them with. D-14 answered DIS-ZYE-002 and 003 with one (`<<| t, m`), so
// the question is now asked in it; the code alone is still judged for 001.
>>| {
    @ _i:1..19 {
        <<| t, m
        >> 0d|t| ":" m " "
    }
}
